# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — NEVER commit these.
#
# `.env` and `.env.prod` hold real API keys (TAVILY_API_KEY, EXA_API_KEY,
# RAPID_API_KEY). Both the plain and the per-environment forms are ignored;
# `.env.example` documents the shape with no values.
#
# Note the difference from `sms-probe/.gitignore`, which ignores `.env.*` but
# un-ignores `.env`. That pattern is right when `.env` is a safe default and the
# per-environment files are the secrets. Here `.env` itself is a secret file, so
# it is ignored too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android / Gradle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
android/.gradle/
android/.idea/
android/local.properties
android/*.iml
.cxx/
**/build/
*.apk
*.aab

# Release signing — never commit; these live as CI secrets.
*.jks
*.keystore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Room schemas are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# `android/app/schemas/**` is the migration baseline: `exportSchema = true` writes
# it, and `MigrationSchemaTest` compares the migrated database against it. Losing
# it would leave migrations unverifiable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloned dependency sources
#
# The clonedeps skill checks out library source here so it can be read locally.
# It is a cache, not part of the project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS / scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log
logs/
